ng is the graph of $y={7}^{x}+4?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we plot the graph of $y={7}^{x}:$\n\n![](images/cd/cd8226319b26b3fef6db6e98efc187b1c474c91bc0252e424151791fda373b95.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y={7}^{x}+4,$ we take the graph of $y={7}^{x}$ and shift it $4$ units up. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,5),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$\n\n![](images/85/85cc1403ab74e2df97669a7c3363d1abddf6d093c358e888a69b655f1ca7450a.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087821 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd63cb30-a236-546e-82ac-08bce09c88f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Vertically Shifted Exponential Growth Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4093346-6cc0-5f63-9423-7b76da2a672f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1d80c585063f3cd30a6ec1f877e0f2add2bf109bc54506e4b6c9e44a7b5019d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390523} {:answer/id #uuid "fd28d0fd-5ee9-586e-ade7-f559ef7573ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/bb/bbdfe3e538e840385c082f16ca2cdfd07a7731c561d05cab6e7a25f487cdf463.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390524} {:answer/id #uuid "be9702e6-d21c-5c09-a96e-1267b5361dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cd/cd11656e3dae8a4976b1051a135b4bead1e5afc4beb21fa7541571892a037500.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390525} {:answer/id #uuid "35b1a419-9084-5fab-a034-b69305bdd882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/66/6674add26b7a15f5b09c53a832d649979484f0ffd41b440069dd5230cd9a5187.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390526} {:answer/id #uuid "724df295-2359-5b8b-ab62-27d9d0e10f5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a3/a30938f3d3af2fd70a0ee9498d7d99973d5386f062f22aaa8a028e9e18b3fb57.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be9702e6-d21c-5c09-a96e-1267b5361dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cd/cd11656e3dae8a4976b1051a135b4bead1e5afc4beb21fa7541571892a037500.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390525} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cb7b8b6-ddf5-57db-b6c9-dfd64245bb49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5100b042-b82c-5834-8756-fafba09daf0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-26815" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of $y={6}^{x}-0.75?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we plot the graph of $y={6}^{x}:$\n\n![](images/29/29d270676a48f4cf40625ef3ec50b0323c9c99389b2a7d080881727eda28de56.png)\n\nTo sketch the graph of $y={6}^{x}-0.75,$ we take the graph of $y={6}^{x}$ and shift it $0.75$ units down. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,0.25),$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-0.75.$\n\n![](images/3b/3b141be99e5c01c70d6f6f04f4adf06741f1dc0fcef80c73b52e3dba1ae44a87.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292685 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c898bbf-004c-5905-a0a0-761adefc8bd8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Value of a Trigonometric Expression Using the Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "078b25eb-c753-58c4-a8bb-c23711fdad11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290671} {:answer/id #uuid "7908b470-d7ec-55b9-b4ab-b86372edd49a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291145} {:answer/id #uuid "820532c3-42ff-5bba-a8ac-2af534fa5f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291181} {:answer/id #uuid "9fdbc26c-f0b1-58b7-b55e-4663ee54eccb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291327} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc2c5b1-4056-55a7-8817-839d1d89caec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820532c3-42ff-5bba-a8ac-2af534fa5f77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291181} :answer-field/id #uuid "d670500b-2a4c-531d-a949-3190b98d3ea6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83f3d502-62d9-5e1b-a7be-52d9144a4c16" :question/math-academy-id "q-26907" :question/problem "Find the exact value of ${(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parenthesis and use the Pythagorean identity.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =[{sin}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})+{cos}^{2}⁡({105}^{∘})]+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={105}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {105}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({210}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({180}^{∘}+{30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘})=1-\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({105}^{∘})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({105}^{∘}))}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292696 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176047 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "542df339-5020-5680-a39c-a1ae161083e7" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "043c68c8-e391-5780-a3ff-6d80dc52b081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290656} {:answer/id #uuid "931ab8d4-be2c-5e4d-92d6-fc6433eec3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291265} {:answer/id #uuid "9767e111-d1e9-5924-9dc2-6f58d60a1d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291290} {:answer/id #uuid "bb01b60e-6bb3-5d81-89d4-9256edcd3ff6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291443} {:answer/id #uuid "d869766d-8d2f-5348-b322-4dd0c0dc459d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "043c68c8-e391-5780-a3ff-6d80dc52b081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290656} :answer-field/id #uuid "c15b4588-e9b5-5b8e-af3b-02394e3239c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69137884-05b3-53be-9c7c-95b53b1ed329" :question/math-academy-id "q-27009" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=cos⁡x?$ \n\n- The function intersects the $x$-axis at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n- The function has a minimum value at  $x=2\\pi .$\n- The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=cos⁡x.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c77bec4ebb04668fbff5176418ed9c09143a8660879fdf523a158c5f109006c.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. At $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ the function intersects the $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement II is false. The function has a maximum at $x=2\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function intersects the $y$-axis at $y=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068829 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5bb394c3-cd7c-523d-88df-b1306d9d528f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Vertically Shifted Exponential Decay Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5145dde8-60d2-54b7-ad8d-2892ff5d3963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a4/a4161037f51b8c4d95037c3ff28d7e6afecb354d4e0fabc22e5dd819bb65b6cc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390533} {:answer/id #uuid "6680ac81-034b-5243-a46f-e14b15ca391f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/a4/a4511ffac1899bdeb512b0b50b50b6a121477f486ef7e2efc83697fd9dddb8d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390534} {:answer/id #uuid "2d7b451c-b477-571c-b8f0-b6b471ddf99b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17